<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yongle Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yongle Emperor was the third emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>, reigning from 1402 to 1424 after seizing the throne from his nephew. He moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, began construction of the Forbidden City and campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. Under his reign maritime commerce reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> through the voyages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor.jpg" alt="Yongle Emperor" width="289" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_assis_de_l%27empereur_Ming_Chengzu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
